<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">scream out my name like you mean it</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Catra auditions for the role of the new antagonist in the hit teen drama show, Wolf Spring. She draws on every bit of anger, hurt and betrayal that still sits heavy in her chest, and she grabs the role easily. The catch? Adora plays the main character. Their troubled childhood looms over them, and Catra is unwilling to even talk to Adora. Because after all, Adora was the one to betray her so many years ago. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora does not expect to walk into the audition room to see Catra right there, after so many years. Even more confusing is still having no idea what she really did to make Catra hate her so much. Adora is happy for her, getting the role. But Catra is infuriating, and just as their characters are at each other's throats, so are they.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When season 5 of Wolf Spring airs, they are all caught off guard by the instant popularity of not only Catra, but the relationship between her character and Adora's. Media, paparazzi and crazy fans shipping them and their characters make a complicated situation even more so.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>ThisWriterD</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mature</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Glimmer (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mara (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Razz (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angella (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Double Trouble (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Scorpia (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Shadow Weaver | Light Spinner (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Alternate Universe - Celebrity</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Enemies to Friends to Lovers</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Miscommunication</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angst</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Misunderstandings</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>scandals</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>media gossip</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Fame</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora is a famous actor</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra becomes a famous actor</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora and Catra are co stars</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Happy Ending</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Hurt/Comfort</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Sexual Tension</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Sex</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Childhood Trauma</rdf:li>
